#N canvas 0 0 760 1180 10;
#X text 12 8 nsf-player - an NSF/NSFE file through nsf~ + nes~;
#X text 12 40 nsf~ owns the 6502 engine and the frame timing and streams every APU register write as `nes <reg> <val>` on outlet 0 - connect it straight to nes~ (the playback/generation split is the same as vgm~ + opl3~);
#X text 12 110 nsf~ outlet 1 = the DPCM channel as a signal: sample data lives in the CPU's memory map and cannot ride register messages \, so nsf~ renders it itself (the vgm~ DAC precedent). nes~ outlet 5 shows only $4011 direct-DAC writes on this wire (the demo kick is one) \, never the sample bytes;
#X text 12 180 messages: load <file> \, play \, pause \, stop \, goto <track 1..n> \, loop <0/1> \, mode <single/seqloop/seqstop/randloop/randstop> (what a track end does\; advance modes need a per-track length - NSFE time chunks or songtime) \, songtime <sec> \, info. Expansion-chip files (VRC6/FDS/MMC5/N163/5B/VRC7) load and play their 2A03 channels\; the load line says so in plain words;
#X text 12 250 demo_nes.nsf ships with the examples - 2 pulses + triangle + noise + a DPCM kick \, same tune as demo_nes.vgm. demo_nes.nsfe exercises the chunked format (NSFE) with a play length and end bang;
#X msg 40 310 load demo_nes.nsf;
#X msg 40 338 play;
#X msg 100 338 pause;
#X msg 160 338 stop;
#X msg 40 366 goto 1;
#X msg 110 366 loop 1;
#X msg 40 394 info;
#X msg 220 310 load demo_nes.nsfe;
#X obj 40 450 nsf~;
#X obj 40 490 nes~;
#X obj 40 540 *~ 0.5;
#X obj 40 580 dac~;
#X obj 40 620 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 260 620 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 480 620 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 40 730 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 260 730 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 40 840 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 260 840 graph~ 200 90;
#X text 12 960 scopes: nes~ channels 1-5 (pulse 1 / pulse 2 / triangle / noise \, then the DPCM line is nsf~ outlet 1 - bottom left \, the kick);
#X text 12 1010 the mix (nes~ outlet 0 \, not scoped) goes through its own gain into dac~ - no internal clip \, dense tunes need headroom;
#X text 12 1050 nsf~ outlet 2 = end bang (NSFE files with play lengths \, when loop is off);
